---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Add Resources From Your Phone"
description: "Set up your phone so you can add a resource to The Fullest Project straight from the Share menu, without copying and pasting."
permalink: /add-to-phone/
---

<section class="py-12 section-warm">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--color-primary);">Add resources from your phone</h1>
    <p class="text-lg" style="color: var(--color-text-light);">
      Found a program while scrolling? Set this up once and you can send it to us straight from your phone's Share menu — no copying links, no retyping.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="py-12">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 flex flex-col gap-10">

    <div class="card p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--color-primary);">On an Android phone</h2>
      <p class="mb-4" style="color: var(--color-text-light);">Takes about a minute. You only do this once.</p>
      <ol class="flex flex-col gap-3 pl-5 list-decimal" style="color: var(--color-text);">
        <li>Open <strong>thefullestproject.org</strong> in Chrome.</li>
        <li>Tap the <strong>three dots</strong> in the top right.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Add to Home screen</strong>, then <strong>Install</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="mt-5 p-4 rounded-lg" style="background-color: var(--color-warm);">
        <p class="font-semibold mb-1" style="color: var(--color-primary);">That's it — here's how you use it</p>
        <p class="text-sm" style="color: var(--color-text);">
          Next time you're on an organization's website or an Instagram post, tap <strong>Share</strong> and pick
          <strong>The Fullest Project</strong> from the list. Our submission form opens with the name and link already filled in.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--color-primary);">On an iPhone</h2>
      <p class="mb-4" style="color: var(--color-text-light);">
        Apple doesn't let websites add themselves to the Share menu, so iPhone works a little differently — you share to <strong>Safari</strong> instead.
      </p>
      <ol class="flex flex-col gap-3 pl-5 list-decimal" style="color: var(--color-text);">
        <li>Open <strong>thefullestproject.org</strong> in Safari.</li>
        <li>Tap the <strong>Share</strong> button (the square with an arrow).</li>
        <li>Scroll down and tap <strong>Add to Home Screen</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="mt-5 p-4 rounded-lg" style="background-color: var(--color-warm);">
        <p class="font-semibold mb-1" style="color: var(--color-primary);">How you use it</p>
        <p class="text-sm" style="color: var(--color-text);">
          When you find something worth adding, copy the link, open The Fullest Project from your home screen,
          and tap <strong>Submit a Resource</strong> — then paste. Not quite one tap, but no hunting for the site.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--color-primary);">On a computer</h2>
      <p class="mb-4" style="color: var(--color-text-light);">
        On a laptop or desktop there's a one-click button you drag to your bookmarks bar. Click it on any
        website and our form opens with that site's details filled in.
      </p>
      <a href="/quick-submit/" class="btn-primary no-underline">Get the browser button</a>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center">
      <p class="mb-4" style="color: var(--color-text-light);">Prefer to just fill in the form?</p>
      <a href="/submit-resource/" class="btn-secondary no-underline">Submit a resource</a>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
